From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Faris Benhaddou <farisbenhaddou@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 09:01:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Mac app: programs of a multi-program application switch in
 one window

The Ezio Collection is four programs (the menu with AC II, Brotherhood,
Revelations and a fourth), and the menu starts a game with ExecuteProgram,
which was a red stub. The NSP build now extracts and rewrites every program
(nx_extract --program / --programs), sizes the heap for the largest, and
packs each into Resources/dm/p<N> with its RomFS (Info.plist DMPrograms).
ExecuteProgram writes the next program and its launch parameter to
DM_PROGRAM_HANDOFF and signals the launcher, which starts the next host with
DM_LAUNCH_PARAM / DM_PREV_PROGRAM (TryPopLaunchParameter,
GetPreviousProgramIndex) and the old window's place. The new host takes over
the window when its window exists (not at its first frame, which left the
Ubisoft logo movie behind the old black window) and the old host yields
activation and exits, so the switch looks like the Switch's: one window, no
app restart.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

Upstream-Status: pending
Reason: The Ezio Collection's menu starts each game with ExecuteProgram, which was a stub: multi-program applications switch programs in one window
Issue: LNPANDY/NX2Apple#483

